  15 red, and they are TWO defects, not fifteen: 8 are the cpufreq instrument (help, the
  unbound $2, and five sides of "it reports success while a core never moved"), 7 are the
  misc backup (the block never re-checks its own file). Everything else in the file -- the
  retire-debug-keeper sections, the no-EDL sections, and the parts of 12/13 that are about
  what the scripts write rather than about what they can detect -- passes at HEAD, which is
  the honest reading: these are FAILURE-PATH defects, not happy-path ones.

4. what this round does NOT show
================================================================================
  * NOTHING ABOUT THE DEVICE. Device is in EDL. Every /sys, /proc, unit, partition and
    address in this run is a fixture; neither new installer has ever run on the phone.
  * The misc partition in this run is a 8 KiB file of random hex, not the real partition, and
    the adb transport is a stub. What is proven is the SHAPE of the check (non-empty + hash
    + size cross-check), not that the real partition is 1 MiB or that the real backup is good.
  * For the record, the backup on this laptop: /mnt/data/zl1-backups/2026-09-17-misc/misc.img
    is 1048576 bytes, sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS says OK, and the whole file is ZEROS
    (tr -d '\0' < misc.img | wc -c -> 0). A blank misc is a legitimate image, not a broken
    backup -- which is precisely why the check has to be size+hash and not plausibility.
      $ ls -l /mnt/data/zl1-backups/2026-09-17-misc/
  -rw-rw-r-- 1 lvyufeng lvyufeng 1048576 Sep 17 14:40 misc.img
  -rw-rw-r-- 1 lvyufeng lvyufeng      75 Sep 17 14:40 SHA256SUMS
      $ cat SHA256SUMS
  30e14955ebf1352266dc2ff8067e68104607e750abb9d3b36582b8af909fcb58  misc.img
  * `install-cpufreq-governor.sh` has still never run on the device, so the claim "the four
    cores move off `performance` at boot" is not tested here -- only that the applier fails
    when they do not.
  * The governor named in docs 95/96 (`interactive`) and its measured idle clocks
    (307200/460800) were measured by hand on 2026-09-22. This harness does not re-measure them
    and could not: the fake cores are files.
  * The three outstanding heat measurements (zl1-thermal.sh --ab) are still owed on the device.

